## 1. Introduction and Policy Statement

### 1.1 Purpose
This Facilities Guide (OPS-007) establishes the policies, procedures, and standards for the management, maintenance, and security of all MedSync Health global office locations. The goal is to provide a safe, efficient, and productive working environment for all **1,200** employees [1] while ensuring compliance with local regulations and optimizing operational costs.

### 1.2 Scope
This guide applies to all MedSync Health employees, contractors, vendors, and visitors across all four global offices: Boston (HQ), London, Berlin, and Singapore.

### 1.3 Policy Statement
MedSync Health is committed to maintaining world-class facilities that reflect our status as a Series D-stage healthcare technology company. Facilities management operates under the direction of the Chief Operating Officer (COO), James Thompson, and is responsible for managing the company's real estate portfolio, which is detailed in the Office Leases document (See OPS-002).

